==Passive effect==
Tumeken's shadow has a [[passive effect]] exclusive to its built-in spell, in which the player's magic attack bonus and [[magic damage]] are multiplied by three from the player's worn equipment (four within the Tombs of Amascut), capped at a total of 100% magic damage, although this threshold is not currently attainable except for within the Tombs of Amascut. This multiplicative effect includes tripling or quadrupling negative magic attack and damage bonuses.

The passive effect is extremely powerful with max mage gear, as it pushes the player's accuracy incredibly high, even when facing magic-resistant monsters such as [[General Graardor]] and [[Commander Zilyana]]. The staff's max hit also pushes higher with the maximum possible magic damage boost, even more than a [[sanguinesti staff]] and a [[Elidinis' ward (f)|fortified ward]]. It still hits lower than the [[twisted bow]] (when comparing both at max boosts), though it makes up for it for being more accurate in such cases.

The passive multiplicative effect does not amplify the [[Void Knight equipment]], [[salve amulet(ei)]], or the [[slayer helmet (i)|imbued slayer helmet]], although Tumeken's shadow still benefits ordinarily from these bonuses. For PvP, in scenarios where Tumeken's shadow can be used against players (such as [[minigames]]), the multiplier does not apply for balancing reasons.

==Charging==
To use the staff's magic spell, it must be charged with [[soul rune|soul]] and [[chaos rune]]s, holding up to 20,000 charges when fully charged. Each cast requires 2 soul runes and 5 chaos runes, costing {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Soul rune|2}}+{{GEP|Chaos rune|5}}|c}} per cast. Players can configure the charges while the weapon is in their bank by right-clicking on Configure-Charges, as long as players have the required materials. [[Aether rune]]s '''can''' be used in place of soul runes but will '''not''' be refunded if the staff is uncharged.

